  "reviewer_notes": "Single application: the whole US cement plant population benchmarked by the ENERGY STAR EPI. Three models extracted: M1 = the updated EPI (Eq. (1), 2000–2008 data, full coefficients in Table 2); M2 = the original 1997 EPI (Eq. (2), 1997 Census/1998 MECS data, only error variance 0.0264 and interquartile ~20% reported, no coefficient table); M3 = the same original form (Eq. (2)) refitted to the new data (Table 3, coefficients given). Energy vector and dependent-variable quantity are defined study-wide (total source energy) and were reused for M2/M3 with requires-inference. C5 metering origin is nowhere described. The 13%/5.4 billion kg CO2/68 million Gj results derive from comparing M1 and M2; recorded under M1.",
